The board may have missed an important function of "for pay" tools such as are being offered by OpenAI under Sam Altman. It keeps traffic down to manageable proportions by keeping out the looky-loos. It appears they set the price too low for the required level of this effect. The income at the prices cited is way too small to make a big impact on a 20 gigabuck company. It appears Sam  Altman got this and the board didn't. This lead to a very costly mistake on their part. The fees are about traffic moderation more than income.

However, one must take note that the Middle East is NOT a place freedom loving people should want to have low level access to and control of things like OpenAI. They have er ideological issues that are very contrary to the official OpenAI goals.

